    fix(lang): SOL-R1-01 — single-line loops expansion splits every sibling; shared-line edit/remove fails loud
    
    Expanding a single-line loops block now genuinely splits every top-level
    child onto its own line (quote- and brace-aware node splitter), so the
    block left behind is safe for later line-based mutation. Editing or
    removing a kind whose physical line still carries sibling declarations
    refuses with a clear ValueError instead of silently deleting them
    (arbiter ruling: fail-loud over span-rewrite, matching the slice's
    reject-over-support posture).
    
    Regression: add -> edit -> remove on a multi-child single-line block
    preserves all unrelated kinds; hand-authored shared lines refuse.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfGCNdAoSqKQ34mKevuF

